+### Task 1: The `spec` reviewer, aligned with its twelve siblings
+
+**Files:**
+- Create: `core/skills/spec/SKILL.md`
+- Create: `core/agents/spec-reviewer.md`
+- Modify: `scripts/validate.sh` (agent-body invariant checks, orphan-agent check)
+- Modify: `core/shared/output-schema.md` (category root)
+- Modify: `manifest.json` (both arrays)
+
+**Interfaces:**
+- Consumes: nothing.
+- Produces: the reviewer name `spec`, the agent `spec-reviewer` with `loads_skill: spec`, and the roots `spec.missing`, `spec.wrong`, `spec.scope-creep`.
+
+**Note on the roster entry, revised during execution.** The first rewrite of this plan moved the `manifest.json` entry to Task 2, on the grounds that it is what makes the reviewer reachable before its `### Spec text` producer exists. Four reviewers flagged that, and the concern is real, but the fix was wrong in two ways: it contradicted this plan's own "every task ends green" constraint by leaving `orphan skill 'spec'` outstanding for a whole task, and it would have failed CI on every push of the branch.
+
+The window the reviewers were worried about is a release cut from a partial branch. That window does not exist here, because all five tasks land in one squash-merged PR. So the entry stays in Task 1 with the rest of the registration, and the mitigation moves to where it belongs: **do not merge or release this PR until Task 4 is complete.** A reachable reviewer with no producer must never reach `main`, but it may exist between two commits on a branch.
+
+- [ ] **Step 1: Add the agent-body invariant checks to the validator first**
+
+This is the highest-return change in the plan and it goes first so the rest of the task is written against it. In `scripts/validate.sh`, extend the loop that already walks `core/agents/*-reviewer.md`:
+
+```bash
+# Body invariants: the reviewer bodies are one 48-line document duplicated per
+# reviewer, and the schema-parity keys above cover two tokens of it. These are the
+# structural lines whose silent absence changed behaviour in review (a body with no
+# nested-subagent bar can fan out; a body with no stack-signals clause ignores pack
+# files the orchestrator still injects).
+BODY_INVARIANTS=("(review-pro subagent)" "## Identity & mandate" "## Output schema (one block per finding)" "spawn nested subagents" "Stack signals")
+for body in "$ROOT"/core/agents/*-reviewer.md; do
+  for inv in "${BODY_INVARIANTS[@]}"; do
+    grep -qF "$inv" "$body" || add_error "$(basename "$body"): body invariant missing: '$inv'"
+  done
+  grep -qE '^## .* findings: none' "$body" \
+    || add_error "$(basename "$body"): no '## <Axis> findings: none' sentinel"
+done
+```
+
